:"Agriculture: other, Individual income tax: credit","url":"https://legislature.mi.gov/Bills/Bill?ObjectName=2026-HB-6438","textUrl":"https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2025-2026/billintroduced/House/htm/2026-HIB-6438.htm","versions":[{"label":"House Introduced Bill","date":null,"url":"https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2025-2026/billintroduced/House/htm/2026-HIB-6438.htm","type":"HTML"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would create a state income tax credit for owners of farm assets who sell or rent those assets to a beginning farmer. It would apply to tax years starting on or after January 1, 2027, and the credit would be limited to the amount on a state tax credit certificate. People claiming it would need to attach the certificate and, for rental deals, proof that the agreement was active.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"MI-2025-HB6431":{"id":"MI-2025-HB6431","passed":false,"number":"HB 6431","title":"Natural resources: floodplains; predisaster flood resilience grant program; establish. Amends 1994 PA 451 (MCL 324.101 - 324.90106) by adding secs. 33709, 33710 & 33711.","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-10-14","sponsor":{"name":"Curtis VanderWall","party":"R","state":"MI","district":"102"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-10-21","text":"bill electronically reproduced 10/14/2026","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-14","text":"introduced by Representative Rep. Curtis VanderWall","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-14","text":"read a first time","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-14","text":"referred to Committee on Appropriations","chamber":"House"}],"law":null,"policyArea":"Natural resources: floodplains","url":"https://legislature.mi.gov/Bills/Bill?ObjectName=2026-HB-6431","textUrl":"https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2025-2026/billintroduced/House/htm/2026-HIB-6431.htm","versions":[{"label":"House Introduced Bill","date":null,"url":"https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2025-2026/billintroduced/House/htm/2026-HIB-6431.htm","type":"HTML"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would create a state grant program to help local governments, tribes, and some nonprofits study flood risks and plan flood-resilience projects before disasters happen. It would fund things like flood studies, wetland and floodplain restoration, culvert inventories, and related work, with grants covering up to 75% of costs and set dollar caps. The department would set rules, review applications, post project reports online, and send yearly reports to lawmakers and the governor.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"MI-2025-SB1210":{"id":"MI-2025-SB1210","passed":false,"number":"SB 1210","title":"Agriculture: marketing; length of time a cooperative may hold the funds of its members; limit. Amends sec. 9 of 1965 PA 232 (MCL 290.659).","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-10-14","sponsor":{"name":"Edward W. McBroom","party":"R","state":"MI","district":"38"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-10-14","text":"INTRODUCED BY SENATOR EDWARD MCBROOM","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-10-14","text":"REFERRED TO COMMITTEE ON NATURAL RESOURCES AND AGRICULTURE","chamber":"Senate"}],"law":null,"policyArea":"Agriculture: marketing","url":"https://legislature.mi.gov/Bills/Bill?ObjectName=2026-SB-1210","textUrl":"https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2025-2026/billintroduced/Senate/htm/2026-SIB-1210.htm","versions":[{"label":"Senate Introduced Bill","date":null,"url":"https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2025-2026/billintroduced/Senate/htm/2026-SIB-1210.htm","type":"HTML"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would change rules for money collected under agricultural marketing programs. It would require any money from those assessments to be refunded to the people who paid it if it is still held more than 10 years after it was received. Programs already breaking this rule on the bill's effective date would have 2 years to return the money.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"MI-2025-HB5514":{"id":"MI-2025-HB5514","passed":true,"number":"HB 5514","title":"Children: other; prohibition of use of certain restraint while transporting youths to certain youth residential treatment programs; provide for. Creates new act.","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-02-05","sponsor":{"name":"Cameron Cavitt","party":"R","state":"MI","district":"106"},"cosponsors":[{"name":"Julie Brixie","party":"D","state":"MI","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Mai Xiong","party":"D","state":"MI","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Denise Mentzer","party":"D","state":"MI","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"John Roth","party":"R","state":"MI","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Kathy Schmaltz","party":"R","state":"MI","date":null,"withdrawn":false}],"cosponsorCount":5,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-10-06","text":"returned from Senate without amendment with immediate effect","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-06","text":"bill ordered enrolled 10/01/2026","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-06","text":"presented to the Governor 10/02/2026 03:08 PM","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-06","text":"approved by the Governor 10/05/2026 09:44 AM","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-06","text":"filed with Secretary of State 10/05/2026 11:14 AM","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-06","text":"assigned PA 111'26 with immediate effect","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-01","text":"REPORTED BY COMMITTEE OF THE WHOLE FAVORABLY WITHOUT AMENDMENT(S)","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-10-01","text":"PLACED ON ORDER OF THIRD READING","chamber":"Senate